      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ square cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant height of the triangular faces:**\n   The peak of the pyramid is 12 cm above the center of the base, and the center of the base is 5 cm away from each side (half the side length of the square base).\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the slant height, the height from the peak to the center of the base, and half the side length of the base:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Slant height} = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 25} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ square cm}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total area of the four triangular faces:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ square cm}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = \\text{Area of the base} + \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ square cm}\n   \\]\n\nThe total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
