    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the total surface area of the pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the areas of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant height of the triangular faces:**\n   The peak of the pyramid is 12 cm above the center of the base. The height of the pyramid (from the peak to the center of the base) is 12 cm, and the base is a square with side length 10 cm. The distance from the center of the base to the midpoint of one side of the base is half the side length of the base, which is 5 cm.\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem, the slant height \\( l \\) of each triangular face can be found as follows:\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 25} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total area of the four triangular faces:**\n   There are four triangular faces, so the total area of the four triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the total area of the four triangular faces.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
